Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:06:08 +0800
Subject: drm/histb: add the write-back taps the mv100 line carries

The mv100 channel exposes write-back taps the v2 driver did not use.
Set them up so a captured frame can be read back from the mixer.
Both taps arm per commit: each carries its own pending flag, the
encoder's atomic check no longer rejects the second job -- completion
is counted against the channel's vblank -- and a job whose block is
still busy stays queued for the next commit instead of stopping the
scan.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 2 files changed, 939 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)


